WEBVTT

NOTE
Waltz for the Moon — the iconic graduation ball dance sequence.
Duration: approximately 1 minute 30 seconds.

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Rinoa approaches Squall across the ballroom and takes his hand, pulling him toward the dance floor.

00:10.000 --> 00:18.000
Rinoa leads Squall onto the floor. He's stiff and reluctant; she coaxes him gently with a smile.

00:18.000 --> 00:26.000
Squall stumbles awkwardly through the first steps as Rinoa guides him across the floor.

00:26.000 --> 00:34.000
Squall misses steps and treads on Rinoa's feet. She smiles patiently as they move together.

00:34.000 --> 00:42.000
Squall finds his rhythm. His movements become less hesitant as they begin to synchronize.

00:42.000 --> 00:50.000
They move together in growing harmony, Rinoa's white dress swirling as they sweep across the floor.

00:50.000 --> 00:58.000
The dance becomes graceful and sweeping. Stars become visible through the open ceiling above them.

00:58.000 --> 01:06.000
Rinoa smiles radiantly at Squall. Shooting stars streak across the sky visible above the ballroom.

01:06.000 --> 01:14.000
They spin in a final elegant rotation as the waltz reaches its peak.

01:14.000 --> 01:30.000
The music fades. Squall and Rinoa stand together under the open ceiling showing a starfield, other dancers around them. The dance is over.
